_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.05147218531711195,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.004049671099860806,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":4.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.013358377389935727,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":33.3,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.10493487612102803,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.07469,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":49.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"TG Therapeutics, Inc., a commercial stage biopharmaceutical company, focuses on the acquisition, development, and commercialization of novel treatments for B-cell mediated diseases in the United States and internationally. The company provides BRIUMVI, an anti-CD20 monoclonal antibody for the treatment of adult patients with relapsing forms of multiple sclerosis (RMS), including clinically isolated syndrome, relapsing-remitting disease, and active secondary progressive disease in adults. The company's development pipeline comprises Ublituximab IV, glycoengineered anti-CD20 mAb for the treatment of relapsing MS; TG-1701 is an orally available and covalently bound Bruton's tyrosine kinase (BTK) inhibitor that exhibits selectivity to BTK in vitro kinase screening; and TG-1801, a bispecific CD47 and CD19 antibody. Its research pipeline includes various investigational medicines. The company has license agreements with LFB Biotechnologies S.A.S; GTC Biotherapeutics; LFB/GTC LLC; Ildong Pharmaceutical Co. Ltd.; and Jiangsu Hengrui Medicine Co. The company was incorporated in 1993 and is based in Morrisville, North Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael S. Weiss Esq., J.D. | Chairman, CEO & President | Age 59 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 399 people. Revenue per employee of $1.5M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, improving at 228%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $162K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["TG Therapeutics, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $9.2B market cap on $616M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +505% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 34% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 23-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The company is burning through $25M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +44.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 4.6\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 10% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 7.5% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.3\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +44.4% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (27.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 297% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.9739382239382244},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 20% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"TG Therapeutics (NASDAQ:TGTX) versus Pyxis Oncology (NASDAQ:PYXS) Head-To-Head Contrast","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/tg-therapeutics-nasdaqtgtx-versus-pyxis-oncology-nasdaqpyxs-head-to-head-contrast.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793992553.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"compa